# Path-scoped review ownership for the tenant registry.
#
# Phase 5's gate. Every tenant file's header has said since Phase 0 that writes
# here would be gated by path-scoped CODEOWNERS; this is that file. The write
# path (src/agents/platform/registry_write.py) already refuses to touch more than
# one tenant file — this is the second half, enforced by review rather than code:
# a PR that edits acme's registry entry needs acme's owners.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO — measured 2026-08-08, still true.
#
# CODEOWNERS only requests reviewers. Making it *block* requires branch
# protection with "require review from Code Owners", and that is deliberately
# NOT enabled here: this repository has exactly one collaborator, GitHub does not
# let you approve your own pull request, so the rule could never be satisfied —
# every merge would need an admin bypass. A rule that must be bypassed to work
# trains people to bypass rules, which is worse than no rule.
#
# What IS enforced on `main` (enabled the same day): a pull request is required,
# and the `check` status check (`.github/workflows/gate.yml` = `make check`) must
# pass. So the gate is enforced by a machine; ownership here is still routing.
# When a second reviewer exists, turn on code-owner review and delete this note.
#
# The owners below resolve to a real account. GitHub silently ignores an owner it
# cannot resolve — a mis-typed team name looks exactly like a working rule — so
# if these are ever changed to teams, verify with a test PR before believing them.

# The shared catalog defines capabilities for every tenant; a change here is a
# platform change, not a tenant one.
/platform/catalog.yaml          @men16922

# One rule per tenant, matching one file per tenant. This is the shape the
# registry layout was chosen for.
/platform/tenants/acme.yaml     @men16922
/platform/tenants/globex.yaml   @men16922

# The write path and its guards. Loosening these is how the one-file invariant
# would stop being true without any tenant file appearing in the diff.
/src/agents/platform/registry_write.py   @men16922
/tests/test_registry_write.py            @men16922
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @men16922
